# Face-pipeline ONNX weights are operator-provisioned at deploy (not baked in).
# Keep LICENSE.* + README under recognition/infrastructure/face_pipeline/models/.
recognition/infrastructure/face_pipeline/models/*.onnx

# Model weights are operator-provisioned on the /data/cache volume mount for the
# runtime-vlm target — never bake multi-GB weights into the build context.
#
# Exclude the artifact CLASSES, not cache directory names. `**/huggingface_cache/`
# and `**/.cache/huggingface/` were tried first and matched nothing: the real
# caches live at $HOME/.cache/huggingface (outside the context) and at the
# in-container path HF_HOME=/data/cache/huggingface_cache, so neither could ever
# appear here. A stray checkpoint dropped under scene/ or the service root was
# the actual unguarded path (ORCH-LAUNCH-01-S1-RA-09 / RB-06).
#
# WHY (Docker .dockerignore glob-depth rule — do NOT "simplify" back to bare *.ext):
#   Docker anchors patterns without `/` at the context root only. `*.bin` matches
#   only ./foo.bin, not scene/infrastructure/vlm/checkpoint.bin. Depth-recursive
#   exclusion requires the `**/` prefix (`**/*.bin`). This is the OPPOSITE of
#   rsync (no slash = basename at any depth). Keep `**/` here; never strip it.
#
# scripts/deploy/recognition-service.sh rsyncs this context to the build VM with
# its own exclude list and does NOT read .dockerignore; keep the two in sync via
# artifact CLASSES (tool-specific spellings) — test_dockerignore_weight_exclusions.py.
**/*.safetensors
**/*.bin
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.gguf
**/*.msgpack
**/models--*/
